WEBVTT

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:25.180
of 30 kilotons equivalent to 30,000 tons of TNT.

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:29.460
Whereas some modern thermonuclear weapons are in the 20 megaton range,

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.540
20 million tons, more than 600 times as powerful as the bomb shown here with a much wider radius

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:37.220
of destruction.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:43.390
In this test, many of the structures damaged by the 30 kiloton bomb were approximately

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:45.110
one mile from ground zero.

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:50.720
With a 20 megaton blast, they probably would be obliterated and comparable damage would

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:54.120
occur out to a distance of at least eight and a half or nine miles.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:59.850
Therefore, while Operation Q was valuable for research and test purposes,

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:07.110
It does not reflect the full severity of today's larger thermonuclear weapons with their associated fallout hazard.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:40.030
At a test site, I covered the story of Operation Q, a program to test the effects of an atomic blast upon the things we use in our everyday lives.

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:59.970
As a reporter, I wanted to see...

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:07.520
Operation Q through my own eyes and through the eyes of the average citizen. I arrived at civil

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:14.040
defense headquarters the day before the explosion was scheduled to take place and checked in at once

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:21.100
with an official for a briefing on the test. To give me a perspective of the entire test layout,

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:26.440
a member of the civil defense staff showed me a carefully prepared model of the site.

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:29.970
He explained the scope of the test.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.980
and the detailed care with which it had been planned.

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:36.190
We begin with the question of shelter,

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:40.290
for shelter might save the lives of those far enough from ground zero.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.180
But what kinds of shelter are effective?

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:47.280
Several types are to be tested, from elaborate industrial shelters

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:52.750
to a box-like family shelter in the corner room of a basement.

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:07.180
In this frame house without a basement, a 4,700-foot line,

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:10.870
we will test a bathroom shelter built of reinforced concrete.

00:03:11.740 --> 00:03:15.480
The entrance door and outside window covering are designed to resist blast.

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:29.210
Loss of power may be one of the biggest problems after an attack.

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:36.290
Power poles, power lines, pole transformers, and complete substations are to be tested by the Edison Institute.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:39.660
We hope to learn the answers to these questions.

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:45.240
How will they withstand this blast? How long will it take to make repairs?

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:48.610
How soon can service be re-established?

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:56.220
One complete transformer substation has been erected relatively close to the shot tower.

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:59.970
The second substation and power lines have been placed at a...

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:12.980
much greater distance from the tower. Two kinds of radio towers are to be tested. One tower is

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:18.870
self-supporting without guy wires, and the other has supporting cables. Both types are very common.

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:28.350
Nearby, a complete radio transmitter will actually broadcast from tape before the shot

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:29.870
to be picked up by radios.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:36.580
the test houses both liquefied petroleum and natural gas facilities will be tested

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:45.280
our questions will the fittings and connections stand the test will there be fires all equipment

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:51.210
is installed and checked by experts from the lp gas association and the american gas association

00:04:52.070 --> 00:04:58.750
this is an 18 000 gallon supply tank partially filled with propane and complete with feed pipes

00:04:59.380 --> 00:04:59.960
Here we go.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:08.940
weighing and storage house and delivery platform have been erected on the test site. I was eager to

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:15.050
learn all I could about the various types of houses to be tested. Five types are to be exposed to the

00:05:15.050 --> 00:05:21.220
blast and heat of this atomic explosion. First, a single-story frame rambler without basement

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:28.100
built on a concrete slab. Second, a two-story masonry home with basement constructed of brick

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:29.830
backed with foreign cinder block.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:34.920
Third, a house of eight-inch concrete blocks reinforced with steel.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:39.760
A fourth is a single-story rambler made of precast lightweight concrete.

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:43.460
Walls and roof panels are joined by steel lugs.

00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:51.450
The fifth, at a 5,500-foot line, is a house similar to one previously tested in 1950,

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:57.410
but a new design provides additional strength at a cost increase of approximately 10%.

00:05:57.410 --> 00:05:59.960
That's the real purpose of testing.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:03.180
these houses to find their weak points.

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:08.830
Through the cooperation of the furniture and appliance industries, household furnishings

00:06:08.830 --> 00:06:10.030
were installed in the houses.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:13.900
Mannequin families were supplied by private industry.

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:24.690
Interior home furnishings, also donated by industry, were complete in every detail.

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:34.720
Textiles and synthetic fabrics were also to be tested.

00:06:39.550 --> 00:06:42.430
Those of mannequins are set up in the open facing the blast.

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:46.870
Each item of clothing and each color has been carefully selected.

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:56.160
As a mother and housewife, I was particularly interested in the food test program,

00:06:56.860 --> 00:06:59.420
a test that included canned and packaged foods.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:18.460
Some foods are to be tested in the house, stored in the usual way.

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:25.730
Foods, including fresh meats, butter, and similar perishables,

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:29.900
are to be tested just below the level of the ground at three positions along the ground.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:35.690
the main test line. This will expose the food to high intensity radiation without risking

00:07:35.690 --> 00:07:42.590
destruction of the containers. Test items include sterilized foods packaged in cartons, metal

00:07:42.590 --> 00:07:50.870
and glass. All will be exposed according to plan to give us the most information. The

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:58.220
night of the actual explosion, or rather early in the morning, finally came. On Media Hill,

00:07:58.530 --> 00:07:59.690
television equipment.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:06.820
was positioned. Reporters, commentators, military and civil defense observers all had

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:14.030
one purpose to study the results of this explosion. At a position a mile forward from Media Hill,

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:25.580
the civil defense field exercise group had assembled with their equipment. A small group

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:29.980
of civil defense volunteers were to occupy a trench relatively close to a group of the

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:37.350
On Media Hill, where I remained, there was hot coffee, last-minute briefings, and more waiting.

00:08:51.790 --> 00:08:54.470
On the silent desert, the test objects waited.

00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:56.920
A minus two seconds.

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:07.780
Twenty-four hours elapsed before we were permitted to view at first hand the results of the explosion.

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:19.180
This is what remained of the masonry house that was not reinforced.

00:10:31.470 --> 00:10:35.650
This is the house constructed of reinforced concrete blocks after the explosion.

00:10:37.560 --> 00:10:41.060
Although the redesigned two-story frame house was severely damaged,

00:10:41.690 --> 00:10:44.990
the structural improvements had strengthened its resistance considerably.

00:10:49.570 --> 00:10:51.970
Basement shelter had offered some degree of protection.

00:10:57.440 --> 00:10:59.900
Reinforced bathroom shelter was standing intact.

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:04.480
beneath the ruins of the house, so this type also offered some degree of protection.

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:15.260
The upper section of one unguide radio tower collapsed from the tremendous force of the blast.

00:11:16.130 --> 00:11:21.270
The guide tower was slightly twisted by a power pole which fell across one of the guy wires.

00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:26.340
Within the concrete radio house, equipment had been shaken up,

00:11:26.940 --> 00:11:29.960
but as soon as power was restored, the transmitter resumed broadcast.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:38.320
broadcasting. The 18,000 gallon tank of liquefied petroleum gas was undamaged. The connections

00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:43.920
were intact. The weighing and storage house was scattered across the desert, but the consumer

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:52.040
size tanks were unharmed. The lines and transformers suffered some damage, but most of the power

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:59.840
poles were still standing or could be repaired. The power substation was not seriously harmed.

00:12:00.380 --> 00:12:04.560
Edison Institute experts tested all lines and found the station to be operative.

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:12.880
Food and cases of canned goods were taken away for laboratory tests.

00:12:19.860 --> 00:12:22.820
Tattoo mark was left beneath the dark pattern of this dress.

00:12:27.440 --> 00:12:29.960
The blast charred and faded the outer layer of this.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:39.470
stock suit during all this activity the mass feeding group had been improvising to feed the

00:12:39.470 --> 00:12:48.160
test observers these cans could have been salvaged from demolished buildings and used for preparing

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:59.890
meat as i watched the people eating i realized that mass feeding would be an important job

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:08.210
for civil defense. I took a last look at the debris and devastation. This time it was only

00:13:08.210 --> 00:13:15.320
a test, a well-planned test, not a real attack. It was a test of the things we use in everyday

00:13:15.320 --> 00:13:26.930
life. Multi-megaton weapons would result in much greater damage over a larger area, but

00:13:26.930 --> 00:13:29.970
many lessons were learned from this test that have affected civil...

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:36.500
defense planning, all these factors must be considered as we plan for the survival of our

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:41.240
homes, our families, and our nation in the nuclear age.
